---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../config/site.js";
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms of Use" description={`Terms for using ${siteConfig.name}'s tools.`}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Terms of Use" }]} />
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-navy-900 sm:text-3xl">Terms of Use</h1>

    <div class="prose-tool mt-6">
      <h2>What this site provides</h2>
      <p>
        {siteConfig.name} provides free image tools, calculators, unit converters, and electrical calculators for
        informational and general-purpose use. Results are provided "as is," without warranty of any kind.
      </p>

      <h2>Not professional advice</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing on this site is professional, legal, financial, or engineering advice. In particular, the
        electrical calculators do not determine safe wiring, breaker sizing, or compliance with any electrical
        code — consult a qualified electrician and your local code for that. Always verify important calculations
        independently before relying on them.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You agree not to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Use automated tools to send excessive or abusive traffic to the image-processing API.</li>
        <li>Upload files you do not have the right to process, or files containing unlawful content.</li>
        <li>Attempt to circumvent rate limits, upload size limits, or other technical safeguards on this site.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>No accounts, no stored personal data</h2>
      <p>
        This site does not require an account and does not maintain a user database. See the <a href="/privacy">Privacy
        Policy</a> for how image files are handled when you choose server-side processing.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, {siteConfig.name} and its operator are not liable for any damages
        arising from use of, or inability to use, this site or its calculations.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        This section intentionally has no content yet: the governing law and jurisdiction for these terms depend on
        where the operator is based and where the site is hosted, neither of which this codebase can determine or
        invent on its own. The site operator needs to add this before the terms are considered complete.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>These terms may be updated from time to time. Continued use of the site after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated terms.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
